*> Implementation test (lane bugmobmove, T30700; 18 sections 3.2 and 3.2.1): the walking speed of standard mobs in blocks per second, measured over
*> 100 ticks of MOBS-TICK on flat stone. The documented steady state of a mob on ground of friction 0.6 is (movement_speed x modifier) squared / 0.454
*> blocks a tick, 20 ticks a second (pig 0.25: 2.75, cow 0.20: 1.76, sheep and zombie 0.23: 2.33). The expected values are computed here from the
*> attribute values of 19 and 20 (independent of the SM-WALK-MILLI table); a mob strolls to a far cell, a zombie also chases a player.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-STDMOB-SPEED.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CITEMS.
 COPY BRWORLD.
 01 WS-NAME                PIC X(16) VALUE "Stefan".
 01 WS-NAME-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG VALUE 6.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PLAYER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(112).
 01 WS-ENTITY-ROW          PIC X(66).
 01 WS-BLOCK-ROW           PIC X(819).
 01 WS-BLOCK               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATE-TEXT          PIC X(5).
 01 WS-STONE               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-TYPE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MOB                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FLOOR               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FX                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FY                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-FZ                  FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-START-X             FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-YAW                 FLOAT-SHORT VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ATTR                FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-EXPECT              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MEASURED            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-DIFF                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PREV-X              FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-PREV-Z              FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-STEP                FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-LENGTH              FLOAT-LONG.
 01 WS-NAMES.
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "pig".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "cow".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "sheep".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "chicken".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "zombie".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "skeleton".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "enderman".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "creeper".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "spider".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "villager".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "vindicator".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "pillager".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "ravager".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "piglin".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "hoglin".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "wandering_trader".
 01 WS-NAME-TABLE REDEFINES WS-NAMES.
    05 WS-MOB-NAME         PIC X(24) OCCURS 16 TIMES.
*> movement_speed x 1000 (19 sections 2.1 to 2.4 and 22.1 and 23, 20 sections 4.1, 6.1, 7.1, 8.1, 13.1, 13.2, 13.6, 21 section 5.5), then the stroll
*> goal modifier x 1000 (the same sections: 1.0 for the animals, zombie, skeleton and enderman; creeper and spider 0.8; villager 0.5; vindicator and
*> pillager 0.6; ravager 0.4; piglin idle 0.6; hoglin idle 0.4; wandering trader 0.35)
 01 WS-ATTRS.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 200.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 230.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 230.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 300.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 300.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 500.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 350.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 350.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 300.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 350.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 300.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 700.
 01 WS-ATTR-TABLE REDEFINES WS-ATTRS.
    05 WS-MOB-ATTR         BINARY-LONG OCCURS 16 TIMES.
 01 WS-MODS.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 800.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 800.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 500.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 600.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 600.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 400.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 600.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 400.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 350.
 01 WS-MOD-TABLE REDEFINES WS-MODS.
    05 WS-MOB-MOD          BINARY-LONG OCCURS 16 TIMES.
 01 WS-PANICS.
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "pig".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "cow".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "sheep".
    05 FILLER PIC X(24) VALUE "villager".
 01 WS-PANIC-TABLE REDEFINES WS-PANICS.
    05 WS-PANIC-NAME       PIC X(24) OCCURS 4 TIMES.
*> movement_speed x 1000 and the panic goal modifier x 1000 (19 sections 2.1 to 2.4: 1.25, 2.0, 1.25; 22.3: the villager's 0.5 x 1.5)
 01 WS-PANIC-ATTRS.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 200.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 230.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 500.
 01 WS-PANIC-ATTR-TABLE REDEFINES WS-PANIC-ATTRS.
    05 WS-PANIC-ATTR       BINARY-LONG OCCURS 4 TIMES.
 01 WS-PANIC-MODS.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 2000.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 1250.
    05 FILLER BINARY-LONG VALUE 750.
 01 WS-PANIC-MOD-TABLE REDEFINES WS-PANIC-MODS.
    05 WS-PANIC-MOD        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 4 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     CALL "TEST-STANDARD-TABLES"
     CALL "BR-WORLD-READY"
     CALL "TEST-JOIN" USING WS-NAME WS-NAME-LENGTH WS-CONN
     MOVE CN-PLAYER(WS-CONN) TO WS-PLAYER
     MOVE 1 TO PL-MODE(WS-PLAYER)
     MOVE PL-DIM(WS-PLAYER) TO WS-DIM
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "minecraft:stone" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-BLOCK-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-BLOCK WS-BLOCK-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE WS-BLOCK-ROW(1 + 4 + 35 + 32 + 288 + 4 + 5:5) TO WS-STATE-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-STONE = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-STATE-TEXT)
     COMPUTE WS-CX = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-X(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-CZ = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Z(WS-PLAYER))
     COMPUTE WS-FLOOR = FUNCTION INTEGER(PL-Y(WS-PLAYER)) + 40
     PERFORM VARYING WS-X FROM -22 BY 1 UNTIL WS-X > 22
         PERFORM VARYING WS-Z FROM -5 BY 1 UNTIL WS-Z > 5
             COMPUTE WS-K = WS-CX + WS-X
             COMPUTE WS-I = WS-CZ + WS-Z
             CALL "WORLD-SET-BLOCK" USING WS-DIM WS-K WS-FLOOR WS-I WS-STONE
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
*>   The player (creative, so no mob targets it) stands near the strip.
     COMPUTE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) = WS-CX + 0.5
     COMPUTE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) = WS-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) = WS-CZ + 8.5
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 16
         PERFORM MEASURE-STROLL
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 4
         PERFORM MEASURE-PANIC
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE(WS-PLAYER)
     PERFORM MEASURE-CHASE
     STOP RUN.

 MEASURE-STROLL.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-MOB-NAME(WS-K) DELIMITED BY SPACE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     COMPUTE WS-START-X = WS-CX - 16 + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-FY = WS-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE WS-FZ = WS-CZ + 0.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-START-X WS-FY WS-FZ WS-YAW WS-MOB
     MOVE 16001 TO CW-TIME
*>   Two ticks to settle on the floor, then a stroll to a cell 34 blocks east (200 ticks left of it).
     CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     MOVE WS-START-X TO EN-X(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-MOB) EN-VZ(WS-MOB)
     COMPUTE EN-DEST-X(WS-MOB) = WS-CX + 18
     MOVE WS-CZ TO EN-DEST-Z(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 200 TO EN-COOLDOWN(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-PATH-TICKS(WS-MOB) EN-WAY-X(WS-MOB) EN-WAY-Z(WS-MOB) EN-TARGET(WS-MOB)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         ADD 1 TO CW-TIME
         CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-MEASURED = (EN-X(WS-MOB) - WS-START-X) * 200
     COMPUTE WS-ATTR = WS-MOB-ATTR(WS-K) / 1000 * WS-MOB-MOD(WS-K) / 1000
     COMPUTE WS-EXPECT = WS-ATTR * WS-ATTR / 0.454 * 20 * 1000
     PERFORM ASSERT-SPEED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test stdmob speed: " DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-MOB-NAME(WS-K) DELIMITED BY SPACE
         " strolls at the documented blocks per second (milli)" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-MOB
     .

 MEASURE-PANIC.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     STRING "minecraft:" DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-PANIC-NAME(WS-K) DELIMITED BY SPACE INTO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     COMPUTE WS-START-X = WS-CX - 20 + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-FY = WS-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE WS-FZ = WS-CZ + 0.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-START-X WS-FY WS-FZ WS-YAW WS-MOB
     MOVE 16001 TO CW-TIME
     CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     MOVE WS-START-X TO EN-X(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-MOB) EN-VZ(WS-MOB)
*>   A mob that was hit runs from the attacker's place (EN-FLEE-X: 10 blocks west of it) for 100 ticks.
     MOVE 100 TO EN-FLEE(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 1 TO EN-FLEE-PLAYER(WS-MOB)
     MOVE -1 TO EN-FLEE-ID(WS-MOB)
     COMPUTE EN-FLEE-X(WS-MOB) = WS-START-X - 10
     MOVE WS-FZ TO EN-FLEE-Z(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-COOLDOWN(WS-MOB) EN-TARGET(WS-MOB)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         ADD 1 TO CW-TIME
         CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     END-PERFORM
     COMPUTE WS-MEASURED = (EN-X(WS-MOB) - WS-START-X) * 200
     COMPUTE WS-ATTR = WS-PANIC-ATTR(WS-K) / 1000 * WS-PANIC-MOD(WS-K) / 1000
     COMPUTE WS-EXPECT = WS-ATTR * WS-ATTR / 0.454 * 20 * 1000
     PERFORM ASSERT-SPEED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test stdmob speed: " DELIMITED BY SIZE WS-PANIC-NAME(WS-K) DELIMITED BY SPACE
         " panics at the documented blocks per second (milli)" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL "ENTITY-REMOVE" USING WS-MOB
     .

 MEASURE-CHASE.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
     MOVE "minecraft:zombie" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ENTITY-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE 0 TO PL-MODE(WS-PLAYER)
     COMPUTE PL-X(WS-PLAYER) = WS-CX + 14.5
     COMPUTE PL-Y(WS-PLAYER) = WS-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE PL-Z(WS-PLAYER) = WS-CZ + 0.5
     MOVE 20 TO PL-HEALTH(WS-PLAYER)
     COMPUTE WS-START-X = WS-CX - 16 + 0.5
     COMPUTE WS-FY = WS-FLOOR + 1
     COMPUTE WS-FZ = WS-CZ + 0.5
     CALL "MOB-SPAWN" USING WS-DIM WS-TYPE WS-START-X WS-FY WS-FZ WS-YAW WS-MOB
     MOVE 16001 TO CW-TIME
     CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     CALL "MOBS-TICK"
     MOVE WS-START-X TO EN-X(WS-MOB)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-VX(WS-MOB) EN-VZ(WS-MOB)
     COMPUTE WS-FX = WS-CX + 14.5
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LENGTH
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 100
         ADD 1 TO CW-TIME
         MOVE 20 TO PL-HEALTH(WS-PLAYER)
         MOVE WS-FX TO PL-X(WS-PLAYER)
         MOVE EN-X(WS-MOB) TO WS-PREV-X
         MOVE EN-Z(WS-MOB) TO WS-PREV-Z
         CALL "MOBS-TICK"
         COMPUTE WS-STEP = FUNCTION SQRT((EN-X(WS-MOB) - WS-PREV-X) ** 2 + (EN-Z(WS-MOB) - WS-PREV-Z) ** 2)
         ADD WS-STEP TO WS-LENGTH
     END-PERFORM
*>   The distance walked (not the progress along x: the path may bend) over the 5 seconds.
     COMPUTE WS-MEASURED = WS-LENGTH * 200
     COMPUTE WS-EXPECT = 0.23 * 0.23 / 0.454 * 20 * 1000
     PERFORM ASSERT-SPEED
     MOVE "test stdmob speed: a zombie chases at the documented blocks per second (milli)" TO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     .

*> Within 4 percent of the documented figure the observed value is reported as the expected one; otherwise as measured.
 ASSERT-SPEED.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-EXPECT TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE WS-DIFF = FUNCTION ABS(WS-MEASURED - WS-EXPECT)
     IF WS-DIFF * 100 <= WS-EXPECT * 4
         MOVE WS-EXPECT TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     ELSE
         MOVE WS-MEASURED TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     END-IF
     .
 END PROGRAM TEST-STDMOB-SPEED.
 COPY CORETEST.
